b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), recursive Boolean procedures with value parameters (4.7, 5.4), the for statement (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), atoms as integer codes and sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: L c1 ... cL, the length and then the messages of the one sequence, each as its code, 1 for INC and 2 for READ. The READ messages bind the unknowns r1, r2 and so on, in the order they come in the sequence;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P14b. run(m, 0), with m the sequence of the stage, by the cases of run, in order, as a Boolean procedure that walks the sequence and gives each READ's unknown its value, the direction the query uses. Case 1: run(the empty sequence, c). Case 2: run(the sequence of INC alone ++ s, c) if run(s, c + 1). Case 3: run(the sequence of READ(r) alone ++ s, c) if r = c and run(s, c), its conjuncts in order. A message that is neither INC nor READ has no case, and run is false for it. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence of hd[c] alone ++ the sequence tl[c]. The unknowns r1, r2 and so on are an integer array, as many as the messages;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, len;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constants: the length, which sizes the cells, and then the messages;
  len := read;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ top, s0, nr, run1, run2, run3;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ ok;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl, rv[1:len + 1];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence of h alone ++ the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ readseq(len);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ len; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ len;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a sequence of len elements, read from the input in order;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j, e, first, last, cl;
    first := last := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ len d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      e := read; cl := cons(e, 0);
      i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ first := cl e̲l̲s̲e̲ tl[last] := cl;
      last := cl
    e̲n̲d̲;
    readseq := first
  e̲n̲d̲ readseq;

  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ run(s, c);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ s, c; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ s, c;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ run(s, c), by its cases, in order;
  i̲f̲ s = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 1;
    run1 := run1 + 1;
    run := t̲r̲u̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ hd[s] = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 2;
    run2 := run2 + 1;
    run := run(tl[s], c + 1)
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ hd[s] = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 3;
    run3 := run3 + 1;
    nr := nr + 1;
    rv[nr] := c;
    run := run(tl[s], c)
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ run := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  top := nr := run1 := run2 := run3 := 0;
  s0 := readseq(len);

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the query: run(m, 0);
  ok := run(s0, 0);

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: every unknown the READ messages have bound;
  i̲f̲ ok t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    PRINTTEXT(`[answer]');
    i̲f̲ nr = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no unknowns')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
      f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nr d̲o̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        PRINTTEXT(`r'); num(j); PRINTTEXT(` = '); num(rv[j]);
        i̲f̲ j < nr t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ')
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the unknowns bound, and the applications of each case of run;
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  i̲f̲ ¬ok t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution: a message with no case of run'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`the count was the second place of run, passed down the recursion, and nothing is held after it'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  i̲f̲ ok t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nr d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind r'); num(j); PRINTTEXT(`]'); num(rv[j]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations run/1 '); num(run1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations run/2 '); num(run2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations run/3 '); num(run3); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
